{
  "account": "plur",
  "background": { "color": "#0A0A0A" },
  "slides": [
    {
      "type": "cover",
      "main": ["THURSDAY NIGHT", "AT HEAVEN"],
      "sub": "The room where drum and bass was born."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "Two DJs. One room.",
        "Every Thursday.",
        "",
        "London, 1991.",
        "",
        "Fabio. Grooverider.",
        "",
        "They didn't headline the night.",
        "They took the late slot.",
        "But the room stayed for them."
      ],
      "sub": "Heaven — Charing Cross Road, London"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "They played dub versions.",
        "",
        "Not A-sides. Not vocals.",
        "The mixes no one else would touch.",
        "",
        "Every week, the crowd came back.",
        "",
        "Something was building."
      ],
      "sub": "White labels. Pure pressure."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "The music moved fast.",
        "",
        "Acid house.",
        "Then hardcore.",
        "Then something with no name.",
        "",
        "Broken rhythms.",
        "Heavier bass.",
        "",
        "They called it jungle."
      ],
      "sub": "1991 — 1993"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "Grooverider went harder.",
        "",
        "Faster tempos.",
        "Rougher edges.",
        "",
        "He coined the term: Hardstep.",
        "Then Techstep.",
        "",
        "He was building something darker",
        "than anyone had heard before."
      ],
      "sub": "Prototype Records — the techstep label"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "Fabio stayed warm.",
        "",
        "Rolling breaks.",
        "Melodic chords.",
        "The side of drum and bass that breathed.",
        "",
        "Two DJs in the same room.",
        "Hearing a different music.",
        "",
        "That tension became the genre."
      ],
      "sub": "Liquid vs. Techstep — both were Rage"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "In 1998, they brought the sound to BBC Radio 1.",
        "",
        "A show that ran for 14 years.",
        "",
        "Grooverider was arrested in Dubai.",
        "Sentenced to four years.",
        "Pardoned after three months.",
        "",
        "He came back to the decks.",
        "The show went on."
      ],
      "sub": "2007 — Dubai. 2008 — back on air."
    },
    {
      "type": "cta",
      "text": [
        "Rage closed in 1993.",
        "",
        "Goldie was in that room.",
        "Kemistry & Storm were in that room.",
        "Everyone who ever made drum and bass",
        "was, at some point, in that room.",
        "",
        "Every Thursday."
      ],
      "strobe": "Save this.",
      "cta": "Save this. You'll need it soon."
    }
  ]
